    {
      "type": "TEXT_MESSAGE_CONTENT",
      "messageId": "166254be-40ac-4204-a135-0645d6fb1fec:assistant",
      "delta": "Signal inputs"
    },
    {
      "type": "TEXT_MESSAGE_CONTENT",
      "messageId": "166254be-40ac-4204-a135-0645d6fb1fec:assistant",
      "delta": " (`input()` and `input.required()`) replace `@Input()` decorators by"
    },
    {
      "type": "TEXT_MESSAGE_CONTENT",
      "messageId": "166254be-40ac-4204-a135-0645d6fb1fec:assistant",
      "delta": " turning reactive properties into readable signals. They are available starting in Angular 17.1.\n\nHere is how you upgrade"
    },
    {
      "type": "TEXT_MESSAGE_CONTENT",
      "messageId": "166254be-40ac-4204-a135-0645d6fb1fec:assistant",
      "delta": " from the legacy decorator to the modern signal input:\n\n```typescript\nimport { Component, input, signal, computed } from '@angular"
    },
    {
      "type": "TEXT_MESSAGE_CONTENT",
      "messageId": "166254be-40ac-4204-a135-0645d6fb1fec:assistant",
      "delta": "/core';\n\n@Component({\n  selector: 'app-user-card',\n  standalone: true,\n  template: "
    },
    {
      "type": "TEXT_MESSAGE_CONTENT",
      "messageId": "166254be-40ac-4204-a135-0645d6fb1fec:assistant",
      "delta": "`\n    <!-- Read the signal using parentheses -->\n    <p>{{ fullName() }}</p>\n  `\n"
    },
    {
      "type": "TEXT_MESSAGE_CONTENT",
      "messageId": "166254be-40ac-4204-a135-0645d6fb1fec:assistant",
      "delta": "})\nexport class UserCardComponent {\n  // Optional input with a default value\n  firstName = input('John');\n  \n  "
    },
    {
      "type": "TEXT_MESSAGE_CONTENT",
      "messageId": "166254be-40ac-4204-a135-0645d6fb1fec:assistant",
      "delta": "// Required input (throws at runtime if missing)\n  lastName = input.required<string>();\n\n  // Derived state"
    },
    {
      "type": "TEXT_MESSAGE_CONTENT",
      "messageId": "166254be-40ac-4204-a135-0645d6fb1fec:assistant",
      "delta": " using computed() instead of ngOnChanges\n  fullName = computed(() => `${this.firstName()} ${this.lastName()"
    },
    {
      "type": "TEXT_MESSAGE_CONTENT",
      "messageId": "166254be-40ac-4204-a135-0645d6fb1fec:assistant",
      "delta": "}`);\n}\n```\n\n### Why this is better than `@Input()`:\n* **No `ngOnChanges` needed:**"
    },
    {
      "type": "TEXT_MESSAGE_CONTENT",
      "messageId": "166254be-40ac-4204-a135-0645d6fb1fec:assistant",
      "delta": " Because inputs are signals, you derive state reactively using `computed()` instead of lifecycle hooks.\n* **Type safety"
    },
    {
      "type": "TEXT_MESSAGE_CONTENT",
      "messageId": "166254be-40ac-4204-a135-0645d6fb1fec:assistant",
      "delta": ":** `input.required()` guarantees the value is present without needing default values, `undefined` checks, or the "
    },
    {
      "type": "TEXT_MESSAGE_CONTENT",
      "messageId": "166254be-40ac-4204-a135-0645d6fb1fec:assistant",
      "delta": "`!` non-null assertion operator.\n* **Better interoperability:** They work seamlessly with `effect()` and `to"
    },
    {
      "type": "TEXT_MESSAGE_CONTENT",
      "messageId": "166254be-40ac-4204-a135-0645d6fb1fec:assistant",
      "delta": "Observable()` when you need to bridge into RxJS."
    },
    {
      "type": "TEXT_MESSAGE_END",
      "messageId": "166254be-40ac-4204-a135-0645d6fb1fec:assistant"
    },
